{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.PhysicalIntractability"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.physical_cost_not_polyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.physical_cost_not_polyBounded","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L74-L84","doc":"**The derived physical cost is not polynomially budgeted (sorry-free).**\nApplying the squeeze to the derived boundary cost: a bandwidth-`B` device\nthat must read the full `3^{3n}` surviving resolution tree has a step count\nof strictly greater ω-grade than every polynomial budget.  This is the\nsurreal `ord_ω(steps) > ord_ω(budget)` statement of\n`qou_physical_intractability_unconditional`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.superPoly_mul_of_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.superPoly_mul_of_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L64-L70","doc":"**Super-poly grade is stable under multiplying by a `≥ 1` factor\n(sorry-free).**  Multiplying a super-polynomial cost by any factor that is\nat least `1` keeps it super-polynomial — polynomial (or larger) dressing\nfactors never lower the ω-grade. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.superPoly_add_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.superPoly_add_left","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**Super-poly grade is stable under adding a sub-dominant term\n(sorry-free).**  Adding *any* overhead `g` to a super-polynomial cost `f`\nkeeps it super-polynomial — the higher ω-grade absorbs the lower.  This is\nthe bound-management fact: overheads never lower the grade. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.mono","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L48-L54","doc":"**Budget grade is monotone / downward-closed (sorry-free).**  Anything\ndominated by a poly-budgeted function is poly-budgeted — bounding a\nsmaller quantity by the same budget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_superPoly_of_polyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_superPoly_of_polyBounded","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L44-L46","doc":"**Dually (sorry-free): a polynomial budget is never super-polynomial.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyBounded_of_superPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyBounded_of_superPoly","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L35-L42","doc":"**The surreal squeeze (sorry-free).**  A super-polynomial cost is not\npolynomially budgeted: `ord_ω(cost) > ord_ω(budget)`. Immediate from the\nDe Morgan duality of the two grades. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PolyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PolyBounded","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SurrealBudgetGrade.lean#L30-L33","doc":"**Polynomially bounded** — the *budget grade*: `f` is dominated by some\npolynomial `c·nᵏ`. In ω-grade terms `ord_ω(f) ≤ ord_ω(nᵏ)`. This is the\nexact De Morgan dual of `SuperPolynomial`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}